------------------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream attributions
------------------------------------------------------------------------

The hyperevm-safety library is built on the following upstream work.
Each attribution carries the pinned version it currently targets; this
file is updated as pins move.

- hyperliquid-dev/hyper-evm-lib — MIT-licensed HyperEVM-side simulator
  of the HyperCore precompile surface (0x800–0x80B) and the CoreWriter
  call site. Pinned at commit
  `6abf28fca081f56c43b0f94af23699f1b43d2329` (HEAD as of 2026-04-24,
  when the T-2 evaluation was performed). The pin lives in
  `.github/actions/foundry-setup/action.yml`; the behaviors depended on
  are documented in `docs/hyper-evm-lib-notes.md`.

- CaliperForge chimera-template-pack — Apache-2.0 Foundry + Recon
  Chimera + Echidna + Medusa scaffold. hyperevm-safety reuses the
  composite action, the `Properties.sol` Recon Chimera bundle pattern,
  the seeded fuzz configuration, and the per-PR clean/planted CI
  discipline.

- endix-foundation-v1/purrkit — MIT-licensed HyperEVM toolkit. The
  T-2 build ticket evaluates whether any specific precompile semantic
  is more faithfully modeled by purrkit than by hyper-evm-lib; if
  files are cherry-picked into `src/sim/`, this NOTICE is updated to
  name each file with its source commit hash. As of scaffold time, no
  purrkit file has been vendored.

